{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3169","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3169","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3169\",\"parent_revision\":\"6822df4d2cbffaf4c41b2b2af7b68ba555ad706d\",\"root_revision\":\"6b9ce36b04c26c17a152ffe880d15af96af1d19da91c4838ede59413ea3e91e0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need duplicate detection exists to serve is: before I spend effort researching and planning a problem, tell me whether that work already exists so I can extend it instead of repeating it. The current check does not serve that need, and each gap is independent of the others.\\n\\nObserved 2026-08-23: three items were created that duplicated items filed one to three minutes earlier by a concurrent session \u2014 #3139 duplicating #3138 (five seconds apart), #3143 duplicating #3141, #3144 duplicating #3140. The check ran on all three and reported no duplicate. Research and planning had already been spent on each.\\n\\n**It matches the wrong thing.** `_check_for_duplicates` in `backlog_core/operations.py` calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, items)`, which runs `difflib.SequenceMatcher` over normalised titles. That is character-sequence similarity on one field. Two authors describing the same defect choose different words, so the titles do not resemble each other even when the described problem is identical. Compare the pair that scored no match:\\n\\n- \\\"CI check for drift between MCP server tool lists and agent frontmatter `tools:` entries\\\"\\n- \\\"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts from MCP server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions\\\"\\n\\nThe capability the need requires already exists in the same package: `backlog_list` accepts `search` and performs full-text matching across title, description, acceptance criteria and every section body, with AND/OR/NOT operators, regex, field-scoped terms, and `match_context` reporting where each term matched. The gate does not use it.\\n\\n**It fires at the wrong point in the lifecycle.** The check runs inside `add_item`, at creation. By then the research and planning the check exists to protect have already been spent \u2014 creation is the last step, not the first. The need is to know before investing, which means the check belongs at the point work is picked up, and its result has to reach whoever is about to start.\\n\\n**Its result cannot be acted on.** The check raises `DuplicateItemError` and the match tuple carries `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)`. A file path is not a handle a caller can use to extend an item, and an exception offers only abort or `force`. To extend rather than duplicate, the caller needs the existing item's reference and enough of its content to judge whether the new information belongs there \u2014 which is the decision the user actually wants to make.\\n\\n**It reads a cache and reports absence as fact.** `GitHubBackend.list_work_items()` returns from the provider-private cache with no remote consultation; its own docstring says so, and the `backlog_list` tool defaults `from_github` to false. So an item created by another session and not yet pulled is invisible, and the check reports \\\"no duplicate\\\" rather than \\\"cannot tell\\\". `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` states the opposite as an invariant: \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results.\\\" That invariant is documented and this read path does not honour it. This gap is separate from the matching gap \u2014 fixing the matcher alone still misses a concurrent write.\\n\\nWhat a working check has to do, stated as outcomes rather than implementation: find an existing item that describes the same problem regardless of wording; run before effort is spent, not at write time; return the item so the caller can read it and decide to extend; and distinguish \\\"nothing matches\\\" from \\\"could not check\\\".\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:40:19.329259Z</sub>\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n### Claim 1: `_check_for_duplicates()` implementation\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- `_check_for_duplicates()` exists at `backlog_core/operations.py:1341`\\n- Calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, existing_items)` at line 1354\\n- Source: backlog_core/operations.py:1341-1357\\n\\n### Claim 2: `find_fuzzy_duplicates()` uses SequenceMatcher on normalized titles only\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- Uses `difflib.SequenceMatcher` at `backlog_core/parsing.py:567`\\n- Operates on normalized titles only (line 553-567)\\n- Does NOT scan full item content\\n- Source: backlog_core/parsing.py:536-571\\n\\n### Claim 3: Return tuple carries (title, similarity_ratio, file_path) and raises DuplicateItemError\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- Returns list of tuples `(existing_title, ratio, item.file_path)` at line 569\\n- Raises `DuplicateItemError` at operations.py:1357\\n- Source: backlog_core/parsing.py:550 and operations.py:1357\\n\\n### Claim 4: Check runs inside `add_item()` at creation time only\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- `_check_for_duplicates()` called only once in codebase at line 1503\\n- Located inside `add_item()` function (line 1468-1544)\\n- Runs at creation time before issue writing\\n- Source: backlog_core/operations.py:1503, grep confirms single invocation\\n\\n### Claim 5: `backlog_list` MCP tool supports search with OR/AND/NOT, regex, field-scoped terms, and match_context\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- `search` parameter at backlog_core/server.py:1982-1997 supports:\\n  - OR/AND/NOT operators (line 1988)\\n  - Parenthetical grouping (line 1989)\\n  - Regex patterns /pattern/ or regex:pattern (line 1990)\\n  - Field-specific search: title:, type:, topic:, section:, body: (line 1991)\\n  - Case-insensitive substring matching (line 1992)\\n- `match_context` parameter at line 2020-2030 returns matches with field, term, snippet, text attribution\\n- Source: backlog_core/server.py:1935-2030\\n\\n### Claim 6: GitHubBackend.list_work_items() reads only provider-private cache with no remote consultation\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- Docstring states \\\"List work items from the provider-private cache\\\" (line 179)\\n- No remote fetch occurs; delegates to `self._reconciliation.list_work_items()` (line 184)\\n- Source: backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py:178-184\\n\\n### Claim 7: backlog_list MCP tool's from_github parameter defaults to False\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- `from_github: ... = False` at backlog_core/server.py:1936\\n- Source: backlog_core/server.py:1936\\n\\n### Claim 8: CLI's `backlog list` has no --search option and --title is substring-only\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- Available CLI options: --refresh, --label, --section, --status, --title, --type, --topic, --include-closed, --filter, --repo\\n- No --search option exists (line 77-91)\\n- `--title` option labeled \\\"Filter by title substring\\\" (line 85)\\n- Source: sam_schema/backlog.py:77-100\\n\\n### Claim 9: Cache-freshness invariant location and wording\\n**Verdict: REFUTED (partial citation error)** \u26a0\ufe0f\\n- The exact quote \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\\\" lives in AGENTS.md:87, NOT in backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md\\n- Item description claims quote is in ARCHITECTURE.md but it is actually in AGENTS.md:87\\n- ARCHITECTURE.md:436 states the same invariant in different wording: \\\"A missing cache record is reported as unavailable data, never as an authoritative empty result\\\"\\n- Citation needed correction: item mistakenly attributes exact quote to ARCHITECTURE.md; it belongs to AGENTS.md:87\\n- Source: AGENTS.md:87 (exact quote), ARCHITECTURE.md:436 (restatement)\\n\\n### Claim 10: Create workflow Step 3 specifies backlog_list with search and match_context\\n**Verdict: VERIFIED**\\n- Workflow specifies at `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:96`:\\n  `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_list(search=\\\"{concept1} OR {concept2} OR {concept3}\\\", match_context=true)`\\n- This is documented as the pre-write duplicate check (Step 3)\\n- Source: skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:91-96\\n\\n### Claim 11: Observed duplicate pairs (#3139/#3138, #3143/#3141, #3144/#3140)\\n**Verdict: INCONCLUSIVE**\\n- No corroborating evidence found in local files\\n- No backlog item records found citing these issue numbers\\n- Unverifiable session observation from 2026-08-23\\n- Source: Session observation only; no evidence trail available\\n\\n## Summary\\n**Verdict counts**: 9 VERIFIED, 1 REFUTED (partial), 1 INCONCLUSIVE\\n\\n**Critical finding**: Claim 9 contains a citation error. The item's description attributes the exact quote \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\\\" to `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`, but this exact phrase lives in AGENTS.md:87. ARCHITECTURE.md:436 states the invariant in different words. The invariant itself is accurate and documented; only the citation location is incorrect.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:36:42.482417Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Duplicate detection matches title characters at write time, so it cannot tell a caller that the work already exists\\nDate: 2026-08-28\\nGoal: Make the pre-write duplicate check actually prevent duplicate backlog items by matching content (not title characters), running before effort is spent, returning an actionable handle, and refreshing before reporting absence.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current duplicate-check implementation: `_check_for_duplicates()` in `backlog_core/operations.py:1341` calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, existing_items)` (`backlog_core/parsing.py:536`), which runs `difflib.SequenceMatcher` over normalized titles only, and raises `DuplicateItemError` on match. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. `backlog_list` MCP tool already supports full-text `search` with OR/AND/NOT, regex, field-scoped terms, and `match_context` reporting \u2014 the capability the check needs already exists in-package and is unused by the gate. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. CLI parity gap confirmed: `backlog list` (`sam_schema/backlog.py` `list_items`) exposes `--refresh --label --section --status --title --type --topic --include-closed --filter --repo` \u2014 no `--search` option exists anywhere on the `list` command (only `merged-prs` has `--search`), and `--title` is single-field substring matching, the same class of check this issue reports as insufficient. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. `GitHubBackend.list_work_items()` (`backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py:178`) returns from the provider-private cache with no remote consultation (docstring: \\\"List work items from the provider-private cache\\\"); `backlog_list` MCP tool defaults `from_github=False`. Confirms items created elsewhere and not yet pulled are invisible to the check. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Documented cache-freshness invariant: the exact sentence quoted in the item body (\\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\\\") lives in `AGENTS.md:87`, not `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` as cited. `ARCHITECTURE.md:436` states the same invariant in different words (\\\"A missing cache record is reported as unavailable data, never as an authoritative empty result.\\\"). Correction needed on citation, invariant itself confirmed accurate. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. The create workflow's documented Step 3 (`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:96`) already specifies `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_list(search=\\\"...\\\", match_context=true)` as the pre-write duplicate check \u2014 confirms the item's claim that the right check exists and is MCP-only, undocumented as CLI-incompatible. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. Existing test coverage for `_check_for_duplicates` / `add_item` duplicate path and for `find_fuzzy_duplicates` \u2014 not yet inspected; needed to scope how much of the current behavior a fix can safely change without breaking asserted contracts. | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:41:09.871592Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: Full trace surfaces ~18 affected systems \u2014 5 core code files, 2 API surfaces (MCP + CLI) each with a facade, 3 test classes locked to current behavior/shape, and a 6-file doc/generated-graph chain (one of which already documents the *intended* search-based mechanism, i.e. an existing doc/implementation mismatch this fix should resolve). All items trace directly to the 5 problem points already given \u2014 no 6th distinct defect was discovered.\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Producers**\\n- `backlog_core/parsing.py::find_fuzzy_duplicates` (~line 536) \u2014 `difflib.SequenceMatcher` title-only algorithm; the interface being replaced/reworked.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_check_for_duplicates` (~line 1341) \u2014 sole caller of `find_fuzzy_duplicates`; wraps it and raises `DuplicateItemError`.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::add_item` (~line 1503, def starts ~1455) \u2014 sole caller of `_check_for_duplicates`; runs it inside item creation, i.e. at write time.\\n- `backlog_core/models.py::DuplicateItemError` (line 561) \u2014 exception carrying `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)` tuples, not an item reference the caller could use to extend the existing item.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py::list_work_items` (~line 178) \u2014 delegates to `self._reconciliation.list_work_items()`; docstring states it reads \\\"the provider-private cache\\\" only. Underlying implementation: `backlog_core/backends/github_work_items.py:437`.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 200), `backlog_core/backends/memory_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 139), `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py::list_work_items` (line 269) \u2014 same protocol method on native-storage backends (no `FileCache`, no remote-mutation queue per AGENTS.md, so not subject to the same staleness class, but any fix to the protocol method's contract must keep these compatible).\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Consumers**\\n- `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_add` (~lines 1690-1730) \u2014 MCP tool; calls `operations.add_item` via `asyncio.to_thread`; `force` param documented inline as \\\"Skip fuzzy duplicate check\\\".\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py::add` (~line 38) \u2014 CLI `backlog add` command; calls `operations.add_item` directly with the same `force` flag semantics.\\n- `dh_core/operations.py` \u2014 re-exports `add_item` (in `__all__` line 110, imported line 1121) as the plugin-wide operations facade; no independent logic but is another surface exposing `add_item`'s current behavior.\\n- `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` (~line 1935) \u2014 exposes `from_github` (default `False`) and the full-text search engine (`_apply_search_filter`, `_tokenize_search`, query grammar ~lines 190-930) that create/start.md's Step 3 already calls, and that this fix should route duplicate detection through instead of title-only `SequenceMatcher`.\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py::list_items` (~line 78) \u2014 CLI `backlog list` has **no `--search` option**, only `--title` substring filter. `sam_schema/backlog.py::merged_prs` (~line 342-344) is the only CLI command with `--search`, confirming the gap is specific to `list_items`.\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Other References**\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_resolve_reference` (~line 1359) \u2014 separate `backend.list_work_items()` call for reference-uniquing at write time; same cache-only-read pattern/risk class as the duplicate check, not itself in scope but shows the pattern recurs.\\n\\n**Documentation**\\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 (~lines 90-110) \u2014 the authoritative documented behavior: extract 2-4 concepts, build an OR query, call `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)`. Also states \\\"Prefer MCP when available; use the CLI for scripting/dispatch contexts\\\" \u2014 false today since the CLI has no `--search` equivalent (problem point 5).\\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` (lines 126-129, 154-156, 177) \u2014 Mermaid flowchart/table already describe Step 3 as `\\\"backlog_list search/filter, title overlap \u2264 2 token edit distance\\\"`. This is a **pre-existing doc/implementation mismatch**: the doc describes search-based detection while `operations.py` actually runs title-only `SequenceMatcher` \u2014 this fix should make the implementation match this doc, not just avoid breaking it.\\n- `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 line 42 (`backlog_add` param table: `force` = \\\"Skip fuzzy duplicate check\\\"), lines 140-217 and 356-411 (worked examples: \\\"Fix duplicate detection before creating new items\\\", `# skip fuzzy duplicate check`, \\\"Fuzzy threshold of 0.85 works well for backlog titles\\\") \u2014 names the current mechanism explicitly; needs updating if the mechanism/threshold changes.\\n- `AGENTS.md` (~line 87) \u2014 states the cache invariant: \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\\\" \u2014 the invariant `GitHubBackend.list_work_items()`'s cache-only read currently violates when used for duplicate checks (problem point 4).\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (~line 436, `file_cache.py` module doc) \u2014 restates the same invariant for `FileCache` specifically: \\\"A missing cache record is reported as unavailable data, never as an authoritative empty result.\\\"\\n- `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `docs/workflow-layers/L1-trace-work-backlog-item.json` (line 139: `\\\"Step 3 Duplicate detection\\\"`), `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` (lines 4-6: node `G8.create.backlog_list-duplicate`, `source_file: create/start.md:Step 3: Duplicate detection`) \u2014 generated workflow-graph artifacts mirroring create/start.md's Step 3 node. Not hand-edited; regenerate via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after any change to Step 3's mechanism or timing, or they go stale.\\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`, `SKILL-GOALS.md`, `CONTEXT.md` (~line 113) \u2014 reference \\\"duplicate\\\" only as a `backlog_close` dismissal reason (unrelated mechanism). Tangential; confirmed via grep they do not describe detection mechanics, no update needed for this fix.\\n\\n**Configuration/CI**\\nNone identified. `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` contains an unrelated \\\"Prevent duplicate runs when pushing to a PR branch\\\" comment (CI concurrency control, not backlog duplicate detection).\\n\\n**Agent Instructions**\\n- `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 (same file as above) is itself the literal agent instruction the `/dh:work-backlog-item create` orchestrator executes \u2014 its `backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)` call has no CLI equivalent, so an agent running in a CLI-fallback or dispatch context cannot execute this instruction as written today (problem point 5).\\n- No `agents/*.md` files reference duplicate-detection mechanics \u2014 grep across `plugins/development-harness/agents/*.md` returned zero hits.\\n\\n**Systems Inventory**\\n1. `backlog_core/parsing.py::find_fuzzy_duplicates` \u2014 core algorithm, target for replacement/rework\\n2. `backlog_core/operations.py::_check_for_duplicates` \u2014 call site, timing/wrapping to rework\\n3. `backlog_core/operations.py::add_item` \u2014 write-time caller; timing issue (point 2)\\n4. `backlog_core/models.py::DuplicateItemError` \u2014 exception shape; needs item-reference carrying (point 3)\\n5. `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py::list_work_items` (+ `github_work_items.py:437`) \u2014 cache-only read; needs from_github consultation or explicit \\\"could not check\\\" signal (point 4)\\n6. `backlog_core/backends/sqlite_backend.py` / `memory_backend.py` / `beads_backend.py::list_work_items` \u2014 same protocol method, contract-compatibility check only\\n7. `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_add` \u2014 MCP write surface\\n8. `backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` \u2014 the search capability duplicate detection should route through (point 1)\\n9. `sam_schema/backlog.py::add` \u2014 CLI add command\\n10. `sam_schema/backlog.py::list_items` \u2014 CLI list command, missing `--search` (point 5)\\n11. `dh_core/operations.py` \u2014 re-export facade for `add_item`\\n12. `tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py::TestFindFuzzyDuplicates` + `TestFindFuzzyDuplicatesEdgeCases` \u2014 ~14 tests locked to current title-only algorithm\\n13. `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py::TestAddItemDuplicateDetection` \u2014 3 tests locked to write-time `DuplicateItemError` raise\\n14. `tests/test_backlog_core_models.py::TestDuplicateItemError` \u2014 7 tests locked to current exception shape\\n15. `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 \u2014 primary agent-facing instruction (point 5)\\n16. `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 flowchart already describes search-based detection (pre-existing mismatch with actual implementation)\\n17. `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 MCP tool reference doc + worked examples naming the current mechanism\\n18. `AGENTS.md` (~line 87) / `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (~line 436) \u2014 the missing-cache-is-unavailable invariant currently violated (point 4)\\n19. `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` + `workflow-layers/L1-trace-work-backlog-item.json` + `workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` \u2014 generated graph mirrors of Step 3; refresh via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after the change\\n\\n**Ecosystem Completeness Checklist**\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible \u2014 `find_fuzzy_duplicates`, `_check_for_duplicates`, `add_item`, `DuplicateItemError`, and `GitHubBackend.list_work_items` all require changes per points 1-4; other backends need compatibility verification only.\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface \u2014 `backlog_add` (MCP), `add` (CLI), and the `dh_core` facade must continue to accept `force` and surface whatever new duplicate-result shape replaces the current tuple list; `backlog_list`/CLI `list_items` need the `--search` gap closed (point 5).\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 `create/start.md` Step 3, `backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` all describe or depend on current mechanics and must move together.\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated \u2014 `create/start.md` Step 3 is both doc and literal agent instruction; must be updated so the CLI path is executable, not just the MCP path.\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated/removed (if replacing) \u2014 decide whether `find_fuzzy_duplicates`/`DuplicateItemError` are removed or kept as a fallback when search is unavailable.\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated \u2014 none identified as needing change; confirm `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` hit is unrelated (verified above).\\n- [ ] Generated workflow-graph artifacts refreshed \u2014 `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after Step 3 changes, so `dh-workflow-graph.json`/`L1-trace-work-backlog-item.json`/`G8-backend-routing.json` don't silently go stale.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:45:23.599619Z</sub>\\n\\n**MISSION_ALIGNED**\\n\\nThe proposed duplicate detection improvements directly address a documented invariant violation and reconcile implementation with stated design principles. Four alignment points:\\n\\n1. **Cache Invariant Compliance (AGENTS.md \u00a787, backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md \u00a7436)**: The documented invariant states \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results.\\\" The current `GitHubBackend.list_work_items()` cache-only read violates this by reporting cache absence as \\\"no duplicate found.\\\" The proposal's outcome \\\"distinguish 'nothing matches' from 'could not check due to stale cache'\\\" directly fixes this violation\u2014a required, not optional, alignment.\\n\\n2. **Implementation/Documentation Reconciliation**: The existing documentation already describes the intended mechanism. `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` (lines 126-129, 154-156, 177) already documents Step 3 as \\\"backlog_list search/filter, title overlap \u2264 2 token edit distance.\\\" The `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3 (~lines 90-110) is the canonical agent-facing instruction and already calls `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)`. This proposal makes the implementation match the documentation, not rewrite it. (Note: This is a pre-existing doc/implementation mismatch; the fix resolves it.)\\n\\n3. **Logical Handoff Pattern (CLAUDE.md \u00a718)**: The \\\"every stage produces a logical handoff\\\" principle requires stages to produce usable outputs. The current exception carries `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)` \u2014 a file path is not a handle a caller can use to extend an item. The proposal's outcome \\\"return the item so the caller can read it and decide to extend\\\" produces an actionable handoff.\\n\\n4. **Workflow Timing Alignment**: The proposal moves duplicate detection from write-time (inside `add_item`) to before-effort-spent (during work pickup). This aligns with the documented need: \\\"before I spend effort researching and planning a problem, tell me whether that work already exists.\\\" Moving the check earlier requires workflow orchestration changes, but this is a consequence of serving the actual need, not a divergence from mission.\\n\\n**Citation**: AGENTS.md (design principles \u00a715-22, cache invariant \u00a787); backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md (cache invariant \u00a7436); docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md (Step 3 documented as search-based); skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md (Step 3 canonical instruction); recent commits (e.g., #3226 duplicate-write ordering, #3194 entry-id collisions) show historical pattern of fixing implementation/documentation divergence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 three duplicates created 2026-08-23 despite the check running\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T12:47:26.046169Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys via /find-cause skill\\n\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n\\n1. **Observed failure**: Three items created 1-3 minutes apart were duplicates, yet duplicate detection reported \\\"no match\\\" for all three pairs (#3139 dup #3138, #3143 dup #3141, #3144 dup #3140).\\n\\n2. **Why 1 - Mechanism does not detect semantic similarity**: `_check_for_duplicates()` at `backlog_core/operations.py:1341` calls `find_fuzzy_duplicates()` at line 1354, which uses `difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, normalized_new, normalized_existing).ratio()` at `backlog_core/parsing.py:567`. This algorithm measures character-sequence similarity only. For the documented example pair:\\n   - \\\"CI check for drift between MCP server tool lists and agent frontmatter `tools:` entries\\\" \\n   - \\\"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts from MCP server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure in both directions\\\"\\n   - Similarity ratio: 0.4683 (threshold is 0.80) \u2014 no match. Different authors choose different words; `SequenceMatcher` cannot bridge semantic equivalence.\\n\\n3. **Why 2 - Check runs after decision point**: `_check_for_duplicates()` is called at `backlog_core/operations.py:1503` inside `add_item()`, which is the write operation. By then (line 1510-1521), `BacklogItem` is being constructed and persisted. The documented workflow in `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:91-96` specifies `backlog_list(search=..., match_context=true)` *before* write time \u2014 the capability exists in the same package but is not used by the gate that runs at write time.\\n\\n4. **Why 3 - Caller cannot act on result**: `_check_for_duplicates()` raises `DuplicateItemError` carrying tuples of `(title, similarity_ratio, file_path)` per `backlog_core/models.py:561` and `backlog_core/parsing.py:569`. A file path is not a callable reference a user can pass to extend an existing item. The exception offers only abort or `force` bypass \u2014 no decision path for \\\"extend existing item\\\".\\n\\n5. **Why 4 - Check reads stale cache**: `_check_for_duplicates()` calls `get_config().backend.list_work_items()` at line 1353. For `GitHubBackend`, this delegates to `self._reconciliation.list_work_items()` at `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py:184`, whose docstring explicitly states it reads \\\"the provider-private cache\\\" at line 179 \u2014 no remote consultation. An item created by another session and not yet pulled into the cache is invisible; the check reports \\\"no duplicate\\\" rather than \\\"cannot tell\\\", violating the documented invariant in `AGENTS.md:87`: \\\"Cache misses are unavailable data, not authoritative empty results\\\".\\n\\n**Root cause**: Four independent structural gaps, each sufficient to explain the observed failure:\\n- Wrong algorithm (title character-sequence matching instead of semantic search)\\n- Wrong execution point (write-time instead of before-effort time)  \\n- Unusable output shape (file path instead of item reference)\\n- Stale cache read (no refresh for concurrent writes)\\n\\n**Fix locus**: Five files require changes per the Impact Radius:\\n- `backlog_core/parsing.py::find_fuzzy_duplicates` \u2014 replace title-only algorithm with semantic search via `backlog_list`\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::_check_for_duplicates` \u2014 move execution point and change result shape\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::add_item` \u2014 coordinate new timing\\n- `backlog_core/models.py::DuplicateItemError` \u2014 carry item reference instead of file path\\n- `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py::list_work_items` \u2014 add `from_github` parameter or cache-staleness signal\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Documented Workflow S Own Duplicate Step Is Not Executable On The Cli Path\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe create workflow (`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`) does specify content-based duplicate detection as Step 3, before the write:\\n\\n    backlog_list(search=\\\"{concept1} OR {concept2} OR {concept3}\\\", match_context=true)\\n\\nThat is the right check, and it is the capability the need requires. It is also MCP-only. The CLI's `backlog list` exposes `--label`, `--section`, `--status`, `--title`, `--type`, `--topic`, `--include-closed`, `--filter`, `--repo`, and `--refresh`. There is no `--search`, and `--title` is substring matching on one field \u2014 the same class of check as the fuzzy-title gate this issue is about.\\n\\nThe same workflow states that MCP and CLI are \\\"two equivalent interfaces to the same underlying `add_item()` operation\\\". For creation they are. For the duplicate detection that must precede it, they are not, and nothing on the CLI path says so.\\n\\nThat matters because the CLI is the fallback when the MCP write is unavailable. In the observed incident the MCP `backlog_add` call was rejected, the caller fell back to the CLI, and on that path the documented pre-write check had no implementation to call. The three duplicates followed.\\n\\nTwo consequences to weigh, beyond the four gaps above:\\n\\n- Either the CLI gains a `search` option with the same full-text semantics as the MCP parameter, or the workflow states that Step 3 requires the MCP interface and that the CLI path cannot satisfy it. Silent non-equivalence between two interfaces documented as equivalent is the defect either way.\\n- `--refresh` exists on the CLI and `from_github` exists on the MCP tool, both defaulting off. Whatever check is performed, it must refresh before concluding absence, or report that it could not check.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"548476862733dc37c436af0fe5d047fdc139b6b9b3f70aaa73f336a3db0ae147\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRQFe7g\"}"}